From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 07:36:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] measure: the MPC enforces the approach corridor 16 m from
 the target

_predicted_terminal_active gates the eleven terminal rows on a half-space,
approach_axis @ (p - port) < 4.5, with no bound on range. Every state on that
side of the plane has the approach corridor imposed on it at any distance,
while normalized_precapture_truth_margins and the environment's violation
accounting gate the same rows on the entry-disc latch. The optimiser therefore
refuses to solve because of a region the task never judges.

Measured statically: crossing the gate plane at a fixed 16.4 m range flips the
worst corridor lateral row from inactive to -4.130, which needs twice the
constraint_slack_limit of 2.0, so the QP reports infeasible and the zero-wrench
fallback hands the chaser to omega * r. On 262001 that is 379 of 387 steps from
t = 0.8 s, reproducing the recorded row of PRECAPTURE_ENTRY_WINDOW_GAP_WITH_F1
exactly; the slack the QP actually demands there is 4.033 and the demanding row
is a corridor lateral facet.

diagnose_terminal_gate.py adds --terminal-gate proximity, which bounds the
half-space by ||p|| <= ||port|| + entry_axial = 6.0 m. Both terms are frozen
task parameters, so the treatment introduces no tunable constant. The 12-seed
sweeps are in flight and no main-table row is restated here.

