From a93330b9b3f648591e5c61ca953ccf4b7db4db8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 08:03:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] measure: the terminal-gate defect is real, and it was not
 costing the completions

Twelve seeds, fixed setpoint, both horizons. Bounding the half-space gate by
range takes QP infeasibility from 1594 steps to 0 at h20 and from 2161 to 0 at
h35 -- not one of the 24 gated episodes ever loses the controller -- while the
force impulse on the commonly completed episodes is identical to 0.1 N s
(192.4 vs 192.4 at h20, 173.3 vs 173.3 at h35). The h35 default column
reproduces PURE_MPC_ROW_VERIFIED exactly: 9/12, 88.5 s, 167.2 N s.

The completion count does not move: 8/12 either way at h20, 9/12 to 8/12 at
h35, and {262005, 262006, 262011} fail under all four configurations. So the
infeasibility was never the cause of the failures.

What the failures are instead: every timeout under the corrected gate ends
parked at 3.00 m -- the desired pose -- with healthy pointing, one illegal
entry-plane crossing, and the latch never armed. The latch only arms on an
outside-to-inside crossing, so once inside, a fixed setpoint at the desired
pose can never re-arm it. That is verbatim the pre-F1 mechanism F1 was
introduced to remove, and both halves of that trade are now measured.

This retracts PRECAPTURE_ENTRY_WINDOW_GAP_WITH_F1 section 3g, and with it the
T8 reading that the learned layer's contribution is preserving lower-layer
feasibility. What survives is sharper: on 262005 the corrected fixed setpoint
spends 930.6 N s, parks and never latches after 1 illegal crossing, while
V2/262200 completes at 282.8 s with 0 illegal crossings. The learned layer
times the entry; the fixed setpoint cannot.

The proximity gate is the diagnosis, not the proposed final gate: it gives no
corridor preview outside 6 m, so the illegal crossings F1 suppressed return.
Every T7/T8 training run was made against the defective lower layer and cannot
be reported as a coupled row until the gate is settled and the runs redone.

