From b72e0e64c3e9849196856dfca1f792525eac5b70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 09:54:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] docs: T7 to T9 review document for third-party audit

Self-contained account of the round for a reviewer with only the repository.
Every claim is tagged measured / inferred / undecided, the four things this
session retracted are listed together with what replaced them, and section 9
names the specific claims a reviewer should attack first.

The load-bearing change: the coupling motivation no longer rests on the fixed
setpoint making the QP infeasible. It rests on a timescale gap -- the decision
that matters is when to commit to entry, which lives on the 152.4 s tumble
period, while the optimiser's horizon is 2 s, and h50 is already 2.22x over
the control period. No constraint formulation closes a 75x timescale gap.

Section 8 puts the one open decision in front of the reader: which region the
corridor constraint should be enforced over, with four candidates and the
measured or derivable cost of each.

